{
  "$comment": "Conformance corpus for POST /api/v1/jobs request bodies. Protocol 1.9 adds `conditions`, the load case (#85): boundary name to the conditions applied there. Validated on both sides as a shape only \u2014 that a name exists in the geometry and that a key is one the capability reads are checked at submit against the geometry and the adapter's declaration, neither of which a fixture corpus holds. So the invalid cases below are the ones the *model* can refuse: a value that is not a number, and conditions that are not a mapping per boundary. The refusals that need a capability live in errors.json, where the partition they belong to is asserted.",
  "valid": [
    {
      "name": "minimal request with default params",
      "payload": {
        "solver": "mock.laplace2d",
        "geometry": {
          "type": "domain2d",
          "bounds": [
            -1.0,
            -1.0,
            2.0,
            1.0
          ],
          "obstacle": {
            "type": "polygon2d",
            "points": [
              [
                0.4,
                0.4
              ],
              [
                0.6,
                0.4
              ],
              [
                0.5,
                0.6
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "request with params",
      "payload": {
        "solver": "mock.laplace2d",
        "geometry": {
          "type": "domain2d",
          "bounds": [
            -1.0,
            -1.0,
            2.0,
            1.0
          ],
          "obstacle": {
            "type": "polygon2d",
            "points": [
              [
                0.4,
                0.4
              ],
              [
                0.6,
                0.4
              ],
              [
                0.5,
                0.6
              ]
            ]
          }
        },
        "params": {
          "resolution": 64,
          "output": "mesh2d"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a load case on named boundaries",
      "$comment": "Protocol 1.9. Clamped at the root, pulled down at the tip \u2014 the cantilever, with the conditions on boundaries the geometry names rather than on axis-aligned edges.",
      "payload": {
        "solver": "mock.elasticity2d",
        "geometry": {
          "type": "domain2d",
          "bounds": [
            0.0,
            0.0,
            1.0,
            0.2
          ],
          "obstacle": {
            "type": "polygon2d",
            "points": [
              [
                0.4,
                0.08
              ],
              [
                0.6,
                0.08
              ],
              [
                0.6,
                0.12
              ],
              [
                0.4,
                0.12
              ]
            ]
          },
          "boundaries": [
            {
              "name": "root",
              "select": {
                "type": "near",
                "axis": "x",
                "value": 0.0,
                "tol": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "tip",
              "select": {
                "type": "near",
                "axis": "x",
                "value": 1.0,
                "tol": 1e-06
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "params": {
          "resolution": 64
        },
        "conditions": {
          "root": {
            "fixed": 1.0
          },
          "tip": {
            "traction_y": -1000000.0
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "no load case at all",
      "$comment": "The default and the overwhelmingly common case: `conditions` is absent, and a capability whose conditions come from its params is unaffected by 1.9 existing.",
      "payload": {
        "solver": "mock.heat2d",
        "geometry": {
          "type": "domain2d",
          "bounds": [
            0.0,
            0.0,
            1.0,
            0.2
          ],
          "obstacle": {
            "type": "polygon2d",
            "points": [
              [
                0.4,
                0.08
              ],
              [
                0.6,
                0.08
              ],
              [
                0.6,
                0.12
              ],
              [
                0.4,
                0.12
              ]
            ]
          },
          "boundaries": [
            {
              "name": "root",
              "select": {
                "type": "near",
                "axis": "x",
                "value": 0.0,
                "tol": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "tip",
              "select": {
                "type": "near",
                "axis": "x",
                "value": 1.0,
                "tol": 1e-06
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "params": {}
      }
    }
  ],
  "invalid": [
    {
      "name": "missing geometry",
      "reason": "geometry is required",
      "payload": {
        "solver": "mock.laplace2d",
        "params": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "geometry with invalid obstacle",
      "reason": "nested geometry validation must run on job requests",
      "payload": {
        "solver": "mock.laplace2d",
        "geometry": {
          "type": "domain2d",
          "bounds": [
            -1.0,
            -1.0,
            2.0,
            1.0
          ],
          "obstacle": {
            "type": "polygon2d",
            "points": [
              [
                0,
                0
              ],
              [
                1,
                1
              ]
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "a condition value that is not a number",
      "reason": "Condition values are scalars. `\"fixed\": true` is the tempting spelling and is refused: the values ride into the cache key, and a bool and a 1 that mean the same thing would be two different solves of one problem.",
      "payload": {
        "solver": "mock.elasticity2d",
        "geometry": {
          "type": "domain2d",
          "bounds": [
            0.0,
            0.0,
            1.0,
            0.2
          ],
          "obstacle": {
            "type": "polygon2d",
            "points": [
              [
                0.4,
                0.08
              ],
              [
                0.6,
                0.08
              ],
              [
                0.6,
                0.12
              ],
              [
                0.4,
                0.12
              ]
            ]
          },
          "boundaries": [
            {
              "name": "root",
              "select": {
                "type": "near",
                "axis": "x",
                "value": 0.0,
                "tol": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "tip",
              "select": {
                "type": "near",
                "axis": "x",
                "value": 1.0,
                "tol": 1e-06
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "conditions": {
          "root": {
            "fixed": "yes"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "conditions that are not keyed by boundary",
      "reason": "`conditions` is boundary name to key-value map, two levels. A flat map loses which boundary a condition is on, which is the entire question this field answers.",
      "payload": {
        "solver": "mock.elasticity2d",
        "geometry": {
          "type": "domain2d",
          "bounds": [
            0.0,
            0.0,
            1.0,
            0.2
          ],
          "obstacle": {
            "type": "polygon2d",
            "points": [
              [
                0.4,
                0.08
              ],
              [
                0.6,
                0.08
              ],
              [
                0.6,
                0.12
              ],
              [
                0.4,
                0.12
              ]
            ]
          },
          "boundaries": [
            {
              "name": "root",
              "select": {
                "type": "near",
                "axis": "x",
                "value": 0.0,
                "tol": 1e-06
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "tip",
              "select": {
                "type": "near",
                "axis": "x",
                "value": 1.0,
                "tol": 1e-06
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "conditions": {
          "fixed": 1.0
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
